          %h2#references References
          %h3#general General
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kenneth+Wilson"}> Kenneth Wilson
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Confinement of quarks
                %strong D 10
                (8): 2445.
                %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevD.10.2445"} doi
                (1974)
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yuri+Makeenko"}> Yuri Makeenko
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Methods of contemporary gauge theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9780511535147"} doi:10.1017/CBO9780511535147
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://books.google.com/books?id=9W-W2w75ulAC"} gBooks
            %li
              %p
                Wikipedia:
                %em
                  %a{:href => "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wilson_loop"} Wilson loop
            %li
              %p
                R. Giles,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Reconstruction of gauge potentials from Wilson loops
                %strong D 24
                (8): 2160,
                %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevD.24.2160"} doi
            %li
              %p
                A. Andrasi, J. C. Taylor,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Renormalization of Wilson operators in Minkowski space
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9601122"} hep-th/9601122
            %li
              %p
                Amit Sever, Pedro Vieira, Luis F. Alday, Juan Maldacena,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Davide+Gaiotto"} Davide Gaiotto
                %em An Operator product expansion for polygonal null Wilson loops
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1006.2788"}> arxiv.org/abs/1006.2788
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            On
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+measurement"} quantum measurement
            of Wilson loops:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Beckman"}> David Beckman
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Gottesman"} Daniel Gottesman
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexei+Kitaev"} Alexei Kitaev
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Preskill"} John Preskill
              = succeed "," do
                %em Measurability of Wilson loop operators
              %strong 65
              (2002) 065022 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0110205"}> arXiv:hep-th/0110205
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevD.65.065022"} doi:10.1103/PhysRevD.65.065022
          %p
            On super-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wilson+lines"} Wilson lines
            via
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integration+over+supermanifolds"} integration over supermanifolds
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C.+A.+Cremonini"}> C. A. Cremonini
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pietro+Grassi"} Pietro Grassi
              %em Supersymmetric Wilson Loops via Integral Forms
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2003.01729"}> arXiv:2003.01729
              )
          %h3#ReferencesInChernSimonsTheory In Chern-Simons theory
          %blockquote
            %p
              See also at
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbative+quantization+of+3d+Chern-Simons+theory"} perturbative quantization of 3d Chern-Simons theory
              and at
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vassiliev+knot+invariants"} Vassiliev knot invariants
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+bracket"} Poisson bracket
            of Wilson line observables in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/3d+Chern-Simons+theory"} 3d Chern-Simons theory
            was obtained in:
          %ul
            %li
              W. M. Goldman:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Invariant functions on Lie groups and Hamiltonian flow of surface group representations
              %strong 85
              (1986) 263-302 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BF01389091"}> doi:10.1007/BF01389091
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p For more see:
          %ul
            %li#GelcaUribe10b
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Razvan+Gelca"}> Razvan Gelca
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alejandro+Uribe"} Alejandro Uribe
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  Quantum mechanics and non-abelian theta functions for the gauge group
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi SU
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SU(2)
              %strong 228
              (2015) 97-137 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1007.2010"}> arXiv:1007.2010
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://www.impan.pl/en/publishing-house/journals-and-series/fundamenta-mathematicae/all/228/2/88942/quantum-mechanics-and-nonabelian-theta-functions-for-the-gauge-group-rm-su-2"} doi:10.4064/fm228-2-1
          %p
            Discussion of Wilson loop observables in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+Chern-Simons+theory"} abelian Chern-Simons theory
            via
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path+integral"} path integral
            arguments followed by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/renormalization"} renormalization
            (such as via
            = succeed "):" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/framed+link"} framing
          %ul
            %li#Polyakov88
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Polyakov"}> Alexander Polyakov
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Fermi-Bose Transmutations induced by Gauge Fields
                %strong 3
                3 (1988) 325-328 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/S0217732388000398"}> doi:10.1142/S0217732388000398
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Polyakov-MPA-1988.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %li#Witten89
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"}> Edward Witten
                , §2.1 in:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Quantum Field Theory and the Jones Polynomial
                %strong 121
                3 (1989) 351-399 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BF01217730"}> doi:10.1007/BF01217730
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://projecteuclid.org/euclid.cmp/1104178138"} euclid:cmp/1104178138
            %li#CosteMakowka90
              %p
                Antoine Coste, Michel Makowka:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Abelian Chern-Simons theories on
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mn 3
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^3
                %strong 342
                3 (1990) 721-736 [
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0550-3213(90)90334-A"}> doi:10.1016/0550-3213(90)90334-A
                ]
            %li#GMR94
              %p
                G. Giavarini, C. P. Martin,
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fernando+Ruiz+Ruiz"} Fernando Ruiz Ruiz
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Abelian Chern-Simons theory as the strong large-mass limit of topologically massive abelian gauge theory: the Wilson loop
                %strong 412
                (1994) 731-750 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9309049"}> arXiv:hep-th/9309049
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0550-3213(94)90397-2"} doi:10.1016/0550-3213(94)90397-2
            %li{:id => "LeukertSchäfer96"}
              %p
                Peter Leukert, Jörg Schäfer, §7 in:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A rigorous construction of abelian Chern-Simons path integrals using white noise analysis
                %strong 08
                03 (1996) 445-456 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/S0129055X96000147"}> doi:10.1142/S0129055X96000147
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li#GuadagniniThuillier08
              %p
